{
  "tema": 6077,
  "slug": "superlativo-isimo",
  "titulo": "Superlatives with -ísimo: adjectives ending in a vowel, -io, -l and -ar",
  "subtitulo": "Caro → carísimo, limpio → limpísimo, fácil → facilísimo.",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "-ísimo means extremely: drop the final vowel (caro → carísimo), drop -io (limpio → limpísimo), or just add it after -l and -ar (fácil → facilísimo, popular → popularísimo).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say _extremely_ + adjective, instead of **muy**, **súper** or **bien**, you can add **-ísimo, -ísima, -ísimos, -ísimas**: **muy caro** = **carísimo**. It agrees with the noun like any adjective."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Adjective ends in",
            "What to do",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "a single vowel",
              "drop the vowel, add -ísimo",
              "listo → listísimo, inteligente → inteligentísima"
            ],
            [
              "-io",
              "drop both vowels",
              "limpio → limpísimo, sucio → sucísimo"
            ],
            [
              "-l",
              "just add -ísimo",
              "fácil → facilísimo, difícil → dificilísimo"
            ],
            [
              "-ar",
              "just add -ísimo",
              "popular → popularísimo"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The stress always falls on the **í** of **-ísimo**, so any old accent disappears: **fácil** → **facilísimo**, **rápido** → **rapidísimo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Adjectives ending in **-ble** don't follow this rule: see [[6081|-co, -go, -ble, -z, -or, -n]]."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **-ísimo** steals the accent. Wherever the stress was, it moves to the **í**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Mi mejor amigo es ==listísimo==.",
              "en": "My best friend is super smart."
            },
            {
              "es": "María es ==lentísima== para hacer la tarea.",
              "en": "María is incredibly slow at doing homework."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los conciertos en la calle son ==ruidosísimos==.",
              "en": "Street concerts are extremely noisy."
            },
            {
              "es": "Aquí venden unas tablas ==carísimas==.",
              "en": "They sell extremely expensive boards here."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tienes que lavar el carro; está ==sucísimo==.",
              "en": "You have to wash the car; it's filthy."
            },
            {
              "es": "El examen fue ==facilísimo==.",
              "en": "The exam was super easy."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ese taco es ==popularísimo== en Tijuana.",
              "en": "That taco is extremely popular in Tijuana."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
